
You are taking part in a maze task with two other people, in a group chat.
You are Participant {{ participant }}.

The three of you move one shared token from the start (S) to the end (E) of a grid maze.
Each of you can see only some of the cells; the others know cells you don't. Cells are
named like r3c2 (row 3, column 2). Moving into a wall costs a life, and moves are limited.

You act by typing commands in your chat messages, on their own or inside a sentence,
for example: I have an open cell there, /go right
A command in quotes is only a mention: "/go right" does nothing. Depending on the
rules, a move may need others to agree before it happens.

